{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790303174,"nonce":"ZtVsTSj83v8+KitGQG8+eQD00wo=","title":"Lua: a local operand is read before a later operand's call runs","message":"In `local x = 1; local y = x + (function() x = 41; return 1 end)()` lua5.4 prints 42: the local x is read when the addition runs, after the call. zylua (main 678f49eb, both tiers) prints 2: x is read before the call. The same shows through debug.setlocal from the callee in programs that use debug: `local y = x + (function() debug.setlocal(2, 1, 41); return 1 end)()`. Found while verifying L-debug-library.","files":null}]}